From: Agent
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Force b_max=1 for eMMC in legacy (SPL) init

SPL on sun50i-h5 uses the non-DM path (sunxi_mmc_init, name "SUNXI SD/MMC"),
not sunxi_mmc_probe(). CMD18 (multi-block read) hangs the controller in PIO
mode, so force single-block reads for mmc2 (eMMC) in this path.

---
 drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
@@ -584,5 +584,9 @@ struct mmc *sunxi_mmc_init(int sdc_no)
 	cfg->b_max = CONFIG_SYS_MMC_MAX_BLK_COUNT;
 
+	if (sdc_no == 2)
+		cfg->b_max = 1;
+	printf("[MMC%d] legacy init b_max=%u\n", sdc_no, cfg->b_max);
+
 	cfg->f_min = 400000;
 	cfg->f_max = 52000000;
 
